$ skills guard-hook
# fields of the envelope it does not read, of the wrong type
--- stdin ---
{"cwd":5,"hook_event_name":7,"session_id":{},"tool_name":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"labdrian skills approve"}}
--- exit ---
0
--- stdout ---
{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"PreToolUse","permissionDecision":"deny","permissionDecisionReason":"labdrian skills approve guard: \"skills approve\" records that a human reviewed the exact SKILL.md bytes, so the agent must not run it. Ask the person to review skills/<id>/SKILL.md and run this themselves in a terminal: labdrian skills approve --id <id> --approver <name>. This guard matches text only, so it is a speed bump, not a security boundary: it matches the command text, so it can be bypassed, and it also denies a command that only spells an entry point followed by \"skills approve\" (reword such a command)."}}
--- stderr ---

